  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 108 AM CDT Sun Jul 12 2026\n\nAn upper level disturbance slowly drifts to the southeast today as \nridging builds over much of the central and western CONUS. As this \ndisturbance and its associated sfc low drift southeast today, some \nlingering 40-70% rain chances remain for western Kentucky this \nafternoon. Overall though it will be drier today with decreasing \ncloud cover and northerly winds. \n\nThis week we transition to a warmer and drier pattern as the high \npressure dome builds and expands eastward. This will lead to a much \ndrier week overall except for some off hand, scattered 20-30% rain \nchances several afternoons. Highs this week start off in the mid to \nupper 80s then begin pushing 90 again by mid to late week.",
